       mmkkffoonnttssccaallee [ --bb ] [ --ss ] [ --oo _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e ] [ --xx _s_u_f_f_i_x ] [ --aa _e_n_c_o_d_i_n_g ]
       ... [ --ff _f_u_z_z ] [ --ll ] [ --ee _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y ] [ --pp _p_r_e_f_i_x ] [ --rr _p_r_e_f_i_x  ]  [
       --nn _p_r_e_f_i_x ] [ --uu || --UU ] [ --vv ] [ ---- ] [ _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y ] ...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       For each directory argument, _m_k_f_o_n_t_s_c_a_l_e reads all of the scalable font
       files in the directory.  For every font file found, an  X11  font  name
       (XLFD)  is  generated,  and is written together with the file name to a
       file ffoonnttss..ssccaallee in the directory.

       The resulting ffoonnttss..ssccaallee file should be checked and possibly  manually
       edited before being used as input for the mmkkffoonnttddiirr(1) program.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --bb     read bitmap fonts.  By default, bitmap fonts are ignored.

       --ss     ignore scalable fonts.  By default, scalable fonts are read.  If
              --bb is set, this flag has the side effect of enabling the reading
              of ffoonnttss..ssccaallee files.

       --oo _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
              send  program output to _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e; default is ffoonnttss..ssccaallee if bit‐
              map fonts are not being read, and ffoonnttss..ddiirr  if  they  are.   If
              _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e  is relative, it is created in the directory being pro‐
              cessed.  If it is the special value  --,  output  is  written  to
              standard output.

       --xx _s_u_f_f_i_x
              exclude all files with the specified _s_u_f_f_i_x.

       --aa _e_n_c_o_d_i_n_g
              add _e_n_c_o_d_i_n_g to the list of encodings searched for.

       --ff _f_u_z_z
              set  the fraction of characters that may be missing in large en‐
              codings to _f_u_z_z percent.  Defaults to 2%.

       --ll     Write ffoonnttss..ddiirr files suitable for implementations  that  cannot
              reencode  legacy fonts (BDF and PCF).  By default, it is assumed
              that the  implementation  can  reencode  Unicode-encoded  legacy
              fonts.

       --ee     specifies a directory with encoding files.  Every such directory
              is scanned for encoding files, the list of which is then written
              to an "encodings.dir" file in every font directory.

       --pp     Specifies  a  prefix that is prepended to the encoding file path
              names when they are written to the  "encodings.dir"  file.   The
              prefix  is prepended literally: if a `/' is required between the
              prefix and the path names, it must  be  supplied  explicitly  as
              part of the prefix.

       --rr     Keep  non-absolute  encoding  directories in their relative form
              when writing the "encodings.dir" file.  The default is  to  con‐
              vert  relative  encoding  directories to absolute directories by
              prepending the current directory.  The positioning of  this  op‐
              tions  is significant, as this option only applies to subsequent
              --ee options.

       --nn     do not scan for fonts, do not write font directory files.   This
              option is useful when generating encoding directories only.

       --uu,, --UU disable  (_-_u) or enable (_-_U) indexing of ISO 10646:1 font encod‐
              ings (default: enabled).

       --vv     print program version and exit.

       ----     end of options.

